WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.312
A materialized view is fundamentally different from a standard view.

00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:07.652
The materialized view stores query results.

00:00:07.652 --> 00:00:11.572
That can make repeated reads of an expensive summary convenient.

00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:15.872
But the stored result can become stale as base tables change.

00:00:15.872 --> 00:00:19.817
Freshness therefore becomes part of the object's contract.

00:00:19.817 --> 00:00:27.037
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:32.352
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:39.246
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
